{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>וַיְהִי בָּרָד וְאֵשׁ וגו׳.</b> Its saying <b>מִתְלַקַּחַת</b> — meaning: for since water and fire are two things that are opposites at the extreme limit, and there is no closeness between them, and when they join together the one that is more abundant overcomes and destroys its fellow — if the waters are abundant they can extinguish it, and if the fire is great it consumes the waters. And HaShem made known that in the mission of HaShem, when He sent them together, the fire was מִתְלַקַּחַת — meaning, acting against its nature, which HaShem had imprinted in it, [which was] not to be taken together with the waters; it was מִתְלַקַּחַת within the hail and leaning upon it to do the will of the Blessed One."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:26:12.008679237Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}